# Copy to `.env.local` for local development and set the same names in Vercel
# (Project → Settings → Environment Variables). Never commit `.env.local` —
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is a full-database credential.
#
# Note what is NOT here: no NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables and no Supabase anon key.
# The browser never talks to Supabase, so there is nothing to leak. The two
# Vapi values below do reach the browser, but as props rendered by the server,
# which means rotating them is an environment change and a redeploy of the same
# build rather than a rebuild.

# --- Supabase -----------------------------------------------------------
# Project → Settings → Data API. Looks like https://abcdefgh.supabase.co
SUPABASE_URL=

# Project → Settings → API Keys → `service_role`. Bypasses row level security,
# which is exactly why it lives here and only here. Server-side only.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Vapi ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Vapi dashboard → API Keys → Public Key. Safe in the browser by design.
VAPI_PUBLIC_KEY=

# The ONE demo assistant, shared by every prospect. Per-practice detail is
# injected at call time through assistantOverrides.variableValues — never by
# creating a second assistant. See vapi/assistant.md.
VAPI_ASSISTANT_ID=

# --- Booking ------------------------------------------------------------
# Where "Book a 15-minute call" points. Calendly, Cal.com, SavvyCal, anything
# with a URL.
BOOKING_URL=https://calendly.com/cutthroughfaster/15min
